{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.AlienDerivation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienDerivation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Derivation.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.AlienDerivation.borelCoeff_compose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienDerivation.borelCoeff_compose","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/AlienDerivation.lean#L125-L131","doc":"**Borel composition = double Borel.** Applying the single Borel\ncoefficient twice gives the double Borel coefficient. This is the\nformal-series face of the acceleration composition law\n`α_{1→3} = α_{2→3} ∘ α_{1→2}` for Gevrey-1 → Gevrey-2 → Gevrey-3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.AlienDerivation.abs_doubleBorelCoeff_le_of_gevrey2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienDerivation.abs_doubleBorelCoeff_le_of_gevrey2","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/AlienDerivation.lean#L104-L113","doc":"**Gevrey-2 taming.** A sequence with `|aₙ| ≤ C · Aⁿ · (n!)²` growth\nhas geometrically bounded double-Borel coefficients: `|dbc(n)| ≤ C · Aⁿ`.\nThe Gevrey-2 analogue of the Gevrey-1 taming theorem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.AlienDerivation.doubleBorelCoeff_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienDerivation.doubleBorelCoeff_add","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/AlienDerivation.lean#L98-L102","doc":"Double Borel is additive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.AlienDerivation.doubleBorelCoeff_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienDerivation.doubleBorelCoeff_eq","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/AlienDerivation.lean#L91-L96","doc":"Double Borel = Borel ∘ Borel: dividing by `(n!)²` is the same as\ndividing by `n!` twice. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.AlienDerivation.doubleBorelCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienDerivation.doubleBorelCoeff","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/AlienDerivation.lean#L86-L89","doc":"The double Borel coefficient: `aₙ / (n!)²`. This is the coefficient\nthat appears in the Écalle acceleration kernel (Borel of Borel). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.AlienDerivation.map_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienDerivation.map_const","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/AlienDerivation.lean#L66-L71","doc":"Alien derivatives kill constants (inherited from Derivation.map_algebraMap). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.AlienDerivation.leibniz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienDerivation.leibniz","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/AlienDerivation.lean#L58-L64","doc":"The alien derivative at ω satisfies the Leibniz rule — this is the\ndefining property, inherited from `Derivation`. Restated for clarity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.AlienDerivation.AlienDerivationSystem.alien","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienDerivation.AlienDerivationSystem.alien","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/AlienDerivation.lean#L56-L56","doc":"The alien derivative at singularity ω. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.AlienDerivation.AlienDerivationSystem.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienDerivation.AlienDerivationSystem.mk","kind":"ctor","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/AlienDerivation.lean#L53-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.AlienDerivation.AlienDerivationSystem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.AlienDerivation.AlienDerivationSystem","kind":"structure","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/AlienDerivation.lean#L50-L56","doc":"An **alien derivation system** on a commutative algebra `A` over `R`,\nindexed by a set of singularities `Ω`. Each `Δ_ω` is a derivation\nof `A` (satisfies the Leibniz rule). ","signatureChunk":0}]}